.env
# Every sidecar of it too. `.env` alone does NOT cover `.env.bak`, and an editor backup or a
# hand-made copy holds exactly the same keys: a real `.env.bak` with a live GRIBSTREAM key sat
# untracked on the Pi on 2026-07-29, one `git add -A` away from being committed.
# `.env.example` is the deliberate exception -- it is the committed template, blank by rule.
.env.*
!.env.example
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
models/
*.tar
data/
.vscode/
docs/
.claude/
logs/
*.egg-info/
*:Zone.Identifier
CLAUDE.md
notebooks/